image in the event of a controversy linked to chemical pollution from substances of concern within its operations or those of its value chain Risks LVMH Sanctions and penalties in the event of non-compliance with regulations relating to substances of concern Risks ESRS E3 – Water Wines and Spirits, Fashion & Leather Goods, Other activities Contribution to the depletion of water resources arising from water withdrawal by the Group’s supply chain, particularly in areas at water risk negative impact materiality LVMH Decline in agricultural yields affecting supplies of raw materials needed to manufacture the Group’s products in the event of a reduction in water resources or restrictions on use Risks ESRS E4 – Biodiversity Wines and Spirits Fragmentation/degradation/loss of terrestrial habitat arising from supply chain operations and the Group’s own operations negative impact materiality Wines and Spirits Contribution to soil degradation across the upstream value chain and the Group’s own operations negative impact materiality Fashion & Leather Goods, Perfumes & Cosmetics, Watches & Jewelry Fragmentation/degradation/loss of terrestrial habitat/deforestation arising from supply chain operations negative impact materiality Fashion & Leather Goods, Perfumes & Cosmetics, Watches & Jewelry Contribution to soil degradation across the upstream value chain negative impact materiality Other activities Hospitality: contribution to soil degradation negative impact materiality Other activities Hospitality & Yachts: damage to sensitive ecosystems (coral reefs, tropical forests, savannas, mountainous areas, island areas, etc.) arising from tourism and the use of boats in these areas negative impact materiality Other activities Direct and indirect impacts of restoration work on the state of ecosystems negative impact materiality ESRS E5 – Resource use and circular economy LVMH Impact connected with the consumption of raw materials across all value chains (including packaging) negative impact materiality LVMH Impact connected with waste production, packaging and point-of-sale advertising throughout the product life cycle (including production, sale and use) negative impact materiality Fashion & Leather Goods, Perfumes & Cosmetics Potential destruction of unsold/obsolete products negative impact materiality Fashion & Leather Goods, Watches & Jewelry Pressure on rare materials used to create exclusive products negative impact materiality Fashion & Leather Goods, Watches & Jewelry Optimizing use of resources by ensuring product longevity (quality, long life cycle, repairability, refill capability, etc.) positive impact materiality LVMH Development of new sustainably designed ranges of products/services and use of more sustainable materials Opportunities LVMH Development of new business models based on reuse, recharging, recovery and resale of products Opportunities 22 • 23 LVM H 2 0 2 4 • S o c i a l a n d E n v i r o n m e n t a l R e s p o n s i b i l i t y R e p o r t"
423.esg.en.2024.pdf::chunk-5681,423.esg.en.2024.pdf,423's 2024 ESG Report,Unknown,unknown,2024,clean_esg_or_sustainability_report,25,26,chunk-5681,19,i r o n m e n t a l R e s p o n s i b i l i t y R e p o r t,social,False,False,"i r o n m e n t a l R e s p o n s i b i l i t y R e p o r t LVM H G R O U P SOCIAL TOPICS ESRS S1 – Own workforce LVMH Financial stability and social integration of employees through employment and payment of an adequate wage positive impact materiality LVMH Fulfillment through work and contribution to well-being positive impact materiality LVMH Development of employability through careers and transfer opportunities positive impact materiality LVMH Due to its worldwide operations, the Group must take care to comply with freedom of association and trade union rights negative impact materiality LVMH Employees’ exposure to physical, psychological or safety risks related to the specific features of the sector and its working patterns negative impact materiality LVMH Seasonal activity potentially leading to the use of fixed-term labor (sole proprietors, temporary staff, employees on fixed-term contracts, etc.) negative impact materiality LVMH Potential exposure to discrimination and harassment throughout employees’ working lives (based on gender, disability, etc.) negative impact materiality Wines and Spirits, Other activities Access to decent housing for temporary/seasonal employees negative impact materiality Wines and Spirits Employees’ exposure to weather events negative impact materiality Fashion & Leather Goods, Watches & Jewelry Increasing the employability of LVMH employees in connection with the influence of the luxury sector and traditional craft skills positive impact materiality LVMH Reputational risk in the event of failure to respect the rights of workers, or to manage health and safety risks Risks LVMH Risk of loss of expertise and rare skills in traditional crafts Risks LVMH Opportunity for influence and growth through traditional craft skills and creative talent Opportunities LVMH Opportunity to mobilize talent by developing an inclusive culture Opportunities ESRS S2 – Workers in the value chain LVMH Financial stability and social integration for workers in the value chain positive impact materiality LVMH Potential impact on working conditions (health and safety, labor relations, living wage, job security, working time, forced labor, discrimination and harassment) negative impact materiality Fashion & Leather Goods, Watches & Jewelry Increasing the employability of workers in the value chain in connection with the influence of the luxury sector and traditional craft skills positive impact materiality Wines and Spirits, Fashion & Leather Goods, Perfumes & Cosmetics, Watches & Jewelry Working conditions (decent housing and access to water and sanitation, child labor in high-risk countries) negative impact materiality Other activities Hospitality, Restaurants: working conditions (decent housing and access to water and sanitation, child labor in high-risk countries) negative impact materiality LVMH Reputational risk in the event of failure to respect the rights of value chain workers or to manage health and safety risks Risks LVMH Risk of loss of expertise in rare artisanal professions Risks LVMH Operational continuity by maintaining lasting relationships with key suppliers and improving working conditions Opportunities ESRS S3 – Affected communities LVMH Boost to the local economy by creating jobs and through the Group’s economic impact (specific to LVMH) positive impact materiality LVMH Contribution to equal opportunity through the professional integration of young people and disadvantaged groups (specific to LVMH) positive impact materiality LVMH Contribution to allowing as many people as possible to access culture positive impact materiality Fashion & Leather Goods, Watches & Jewelry Preserving expertise and traditional craftsmanship (specific to LVMH) positive impact materiality Wines and Spirits, Fashion & Leather Goods, Perfumes & Cosmetics, Watches & Jewelry Conflicts of use (access to water and soil) and upstream water and soil pollution in the mining and agriculture value chains negative impact materiality Fashion & Leather Goods, Perfumes & Cosmetics Use of cultural codes/elements belonging to communities negative impact materiality LVMH Improved brand image related to the promotion of traditional craft skills (specific to LVMH) Opportunities"
