ric numerator (Gross global combined Scope 1 and 2 emissions, metric tons CO2e) 765789 (7.45.3) Metric denominator Select from: ☑ unit total revenue (7.45.4) Metric denominator: Unit total 65446 (7.45.5) Scope 2 figure used 150 Select from: ☑ Location-based (7.45.6) % change from previous year 19.73 (7.45.7) Direction of change Select from: ☑ Decreased (7.45.8) Reasons for change Select all that apply ☑ Change in renewable energy consumption ☑ Other emissions reduction activities ☑ Change in revenue (7.45.9) Please explain CO2 emissions increase related to production ramp-up have been neutralized by energy efficiency projects, improvement of emissions factor, increased level of renewable energies (Electricity, Biomethane and SAF), also Revenues have increased Row 2 (7.45.1) Intensity figure 831.221 (7.45.2) Metric numerator (Gross global combined Scope 1 and 2 emissions, metric tons CO2e) 610947 (7.45.3) Metric denominator 151"
2025_climate_report_9706fb9c.pdf::chunk-7409,2025_climate_report_9706fb9c.pdf,9706fb9c's 2025 Climate Report,Airbus,aerospace,2025,long_doc,152,155,chunk-7409,69,,environmental,True,False,"SAF), also Revenues have increased Row 2 (7.45.1) Intensity figure 831.221 (7.45.2) Metric numerator (Gross global combined Scope 1 and 2 emissions, metric tons CO2e) 610947 (7.45.3) Metric denominator 151 Select from: ☑ vehicle produced (7.45.4) Metric denominator: Unit total 735 (7.45.5) Scope 2 figure used Select from: ☑ Location-based (7.45.6) % change from previous year 17.5 (7.45.7) Direction of change Select from: ☑ Decreased (7.45.8) Reasons for change Select all that apply ☑ Change in renewable energy consumption ☑ Other emissions reduction activities ☑ Other, please specify :increased deliveries compared to previous year (7.45.9) Please explain The ratio is calculated by taking Emissions Scope 1 and Scope 2 (location based) of Airbus Commercial and dividing the amount by the Number of Airbus Commercial aircraft deliveries. CO2 emissions increase related to production ramp-up have been neutralized by energy efficiency projects, improvement of emissions factor, increased level of renewable energies (Electricity, Biomethane and SAF), also Aircraft produced have increased [Add row] 152 (7.50) Provide primary intensity metrics that are appropriate to your indirect emissions in Scope 3 Category 11: Use of sold products from transport. Row 1 (7.50.1) Activity Select from: ☑ Aviation (7.50.2) Emissions intensity figure 0.0000629 (7.50.3) Metric numerator (Scope 3 emissions: use of sold products) in Metric tons CO2e 464136000 (7.50.4) Metric denominator Select from: ☑ p.km (7.50.5) Metric denominator: Unit total 7378950715421 (7.50.6) % change from previous year -2.33 (7.50.7) Vehicle unit sales in reporting year 735 153 (7.50.8) Vehicle lifetime in years 22 (7.50.9) Annual distance in km or miles (unit specified by column 4) 2397816.27 (7.50.10) Load factor 82.5% (Reference IATA Average for 2019) (7.50.11) Please explain the changes, and relevant standards/methodologies used Efficiency metric relevant for commercial aircraft products only. All numbers are for commercial aircraft products only. Emissions considered for this calculation are total direct emissions arising from products delivered in 2023 over their entire lifetime as per the scope 3 “use of sold product” calculation. Please note that the absolute scope 3 figure reported in C6.5 includes indirect emissions linked to fuel production, whereas this efficiency metric only includes direct emissions. 2023 data: efficiency metric 62.9gCO2/pax.km, total direct emissions 464,136,000 tCO2e, total pax.km 7,378,950,715,421.3 The decrease of the value compared to the previous year (2022) can be attributed to a higher proportion of latest generation products (A320neo, A350 XWB, A330neo,A220) versus the outgoing generation (A320 CEO, A330 CEO, A380), improving the overall efficiency of the delivered fleet. [Add row]"
