2024_thematic_report_24be3308.pdf::chunk-13168,2024_thematic_report_24be3308.pdf,Thematic 24be3308's 2024 Report,Danone,food_beverage,2024,short_doc,1,1,chunk-13168,3,S T H R I V I N G P E O P L E,,False,False,S T H R I V I N G P E O P L E & C O M M U N I T I E S F O R C O N S U M E R & P A T I E N T S P R O G R E S S & L E A D H E A L T H T H R O U G H F O O D P R E S E R V E & R E G E N E R A T E N A T U R E
2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf::chunk-13237,2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf,C3cd8894's 2025 Integrated Report,Danone,food_beverage,2025,integrated_or_annual_report,1,2,chunk-13237,1,2025 Danone’s performance and impact ANNUAL INTEGRATED REPORT APRIL 2026,governance,False,True,"2025 Danone’s performance and impact ANNUAL INTEGRATED REPORT APRIL 2026 ABOUT THIS REPORT This report presents an integrated view of how Danone creates value for its stakeholders, for society, and for the planet. It brings together financial performance, operational achievements, and sustainability progress that reflects the interconnected nature of our business model. Sustainability is not treated as a separate agenda at Danone. The issues addressed in these pages, from nutrition and climate action to farmer livelihoods and packaging circularity, are embedded in our strategy, our governance, and our daily operations. They shape how we source ingredients, design products, run factories, and engage with communities. This report demonstrates that our commitment to both performance and impact is not a choice between two priorities, but the foundation of how we do business. The material topics covered here have been identified through ongoing dialogue with stakeholders and assessment of impact, risks and opportunities across our value chain. They represent the areas where Danone can make the most meaningful contribution, and where our long-term success depends on getting it right. The 2025 Integrated Annual Report was created by Danone’s Sustainability Performance and Transformation teams, with the support and supervision of the relevant thematic expert teams, who were instrumental in ensuring its achievement, as well as data collection and key testimonies. METHODOLOGY AND ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS TA B LE O F C O N TE N T S GOVERNANCE P.49 PEOPLE & COMMUNITIES P.40 NATURE P.25 HEALTH THROUGH FOOD P.14 PURPOSE, VISION AND STRATEGY P.4 EDITORIAL P.3 2"
2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf::chunk-13238,2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf,C3cd8894's 2025 Integrated Report,Danone,food_beverage,2025,integrated_or_annual_report,2,3,chunk-13238,2,,social,False,True,"LE O F C O N TE N T S GOVERNANCE P.49 PEOPLE & COMMUNITIES P.40 NATURE P.25 HEALTH THROUGH FOOD P.14 PURPOSE, VISION AND STRATEGY P.4 EDITORIAL P.3 2 AN TO IN E DE S AI NT -A FF RI QU E DA NO NE C EO Dear readers, 2025 has been another year of quality delivery and meaningful progress for Danone. We delivered a strong +4.5% like-for-like sales growth. And importantly, we achieved it while driving sustainability in a focused and impactful way, because it is essential to the longterm resilience of our business. In a volatile world, our performance reflects the strength and resilience of our unique health-focused portfolio. Health Through Food has never been more relevant. The food industry is at a tipping point: everywhere, people increasingly understand interconnection between what they eat and how they live. Our categories are uniquely positioned to take advantage of it. In 2025, we deployed Renew Danone Chapter 2 at pace: we continued doubling down on the fundamentals, while further transforming the business. We continued strengthening the capabilities that truly differentiate Danone and kept building differentiation through science. The cutting-edge OneBiome research Laboratory we opened in Paris-Saclay is testimony of it. We moved to the forefront of acquisitions with the purchase of Kate Farms, first doctor-recommended plant-based brand in the U.S. and The Akkermansia Company detaining a strain clinically demonstrated to reinforce the gut barrier. We kept reinvesting behind our brands. Our cross categories partnership with Carlos Alcaraz is an example. We keep investing in our people, growing the next generation of leaders. Through initiatives such as DanSkills, we are upskilling our teams with the critical capabilities of tomorrow — from digital and AI to sustainability, science and leadership. In 2025, we were proud of our significant progress across all targets of the three pillars of our Danone Impact Journey: Health, Nature, and People & Communities. We have this year again the healthiest portfolio in the industry and we are ranked #1 by the Access to Nutrition Index. We have also significantly reduced sugars in kids’ dairy and plant-based products. We were again recognized with a Triple A rating by CDP, placing us among only 23 companies worldwide achieving this distinction across climate change, water stewardship, and forest preservation. Achieving worldwide B Corp certification marked another milestone, celebrating a decade-long journey and reaffirming our belief to combining performance and positive impact. These achievements reflect the relevance of our strategy, the dedication of our people, and the trust of our partners. Together, we are building a healthier future—step by step, anchored in science, with purpose and impact at the core. Thank you, to all the Danoners and to all our partners - farmers, entrepreneurs, suppliers - for making 2025 a great milestone! And thank you to our customers and patients for trusting us every day again. Our priority has been – and will always remain – to serve you with safe and high‑quality products because trust, quality and food safety are strategic enablers of long‑term growth and resilience for Danone. Looking at 2026, we remain focus on disciplined execution — scaling what works well while keeping a constructively dissatisfied mindset. 2026 marks the launch of the next phase of our sustainability roadmap, setting out enhanced health and sustainability ambitions through 2030. Building on the consistent progress achieved against our 2025 goals, this new phase reinforces our strategy to drive long-term resilience, competitiveness, and sustainable growth. EDITORIAL 3"
2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf::chunk-13239,2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf,C3cd8894's 2025 Integrated Report,Danone,food_beverage,2025,integrated_or_annual_report,3,5,chunk-13239,3,C H A PT ER O NE D A N O N E,social,False,False,"sustainability ambitions through 2030. Building on the consistent progress achieved against our 2025 goals, this new phase reinforces our strategy to drive long-term resilience, competitiveness, and sustainable growth. EDITORIAL 3 C H A PT ER O NE D A N O N E P U R P O S E , V I S I O N & S T R A T E G Y VISION HEALTH NATURE PEOPLE & COMMUNITIES GOVERNANCE INTEGRATED ANNUAL REPORT 2025 4 Danone’s purpose is rooted in the conviction of its founder that business should be a force for positive change. A LEGACY OF PURPOSE The essence of the Dual Project lives on in our corporate mission today: TO BRING HEALTH THROUGH FOOD TO AS MANY PEOPLE AS POSSIBLE. This is not a tagline. It is the organizing principle that guides our strategy, our employees, our investments, and our choices, re-enforcing the foundational elements of who we are: a science-based, consumer and patient-centric company, with and by people. Société à mission In 2020, Danone was the first listed company to adopt the ""Société à Mission"" legal status. This was more than a symbolic gesture : it meant embedding our purpose into our by-laws, making it legally binding, and creating governance structures to ensure accountability on these four objectives : • Impact people’s health locally, with a portfolio of healthier products, with brands encouraging better nutritional choices and by promoting better dietary habits. • Preserve and renew the planet’s resources, by supporting regenerative agriculture, protecting the water cycle and strengthening the circular economy of packaging, across its entire ecosystem, in order to contribute to the fight against climate change. • Empower Danone’s people to create new futures: building on a unique social innovation heritage, give each employee the opportunity to impact the decisions of the Company, both locally and globally. • Foster inclusive growth, by ensuring equal opportunities within the Company, supporting the most vulnerable partners in its ecosystem and developing everyday products accessible to as many people as possible. In 1919, Isaac Carasso founded Danone in Barcelona with a simple but powerful idea: yogurt made with cultures from the Pasteur Institute could help children suffering from intestinal infections. His work was rooted in science and driven by a desire to improve health through food. In the 1890s, Nutricia was pioneering discoveries that would change lives across continents, applying cutting-edge science to address nutritional challenges. Decades later, in 1972, Antoine Riboud delivered a landmark speech in Marseille that would define Danone’s identity for generations. He introduced the concept of the Dual Project: the belief that a company could pursue economic success and social progress simultaneously, that profitability and positive impact were not only compatible but mutually reinforcing. This philosophy became the foundation of Danone’s global expansion. D A N O N E"
2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf::chunk-13240,2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf,C3cd8894's 2025 Integrated Report,Danone,food_beverage,2025,integrated_or_annual_report,5,6,chunk-13240,4,F O U N D E R A N T O I N E,social,False,True,"social progress simultaneously, that profitability and positive impact were not only compatible but mutually reinforcing. This philosophy became the foundation of Danone’s global expansion. D A N O N E F O U N D E R A N T O I N E R I B O U D A company’s responsibility doesn’t stop at the factory gate or the office door. The jobs we create, the economic and social conditions in which people live and work, the environment we affect—all these things matter as much as profit and loss. Marseille, 1972 VISION HEALTH NATURE PEOPLE & COMMUNITIES GOVERNANCE INTEGRATED ANNUAL REPORT 2025 5 FROM PAST TO PRESENT Over the past decades, consumer lifestyles and tastes have evolved dramatically and so has Danone: innovating to anticipate needs, adapting products to local contexts, and expanding into new categories and geographies. What has remained constant is our commitment to our purpose. 1966 Antoine Riboud founded Boussois-Souchon- Neuvesel (BSN), historically a glass manufacturer. It diversified into the food industry, becoming the leader in France in beverages and infant nutrition with the acquisition of brands such as evian and Blédina. 1991 The dream of international expansion came true when BSN-Gervais International set up operations in Asia. 2007 The acquisition of Royal Numico, bringing unparalleled health expertise on infant and medical nutrition, completes the transformation to Danone into a health- through food company. 2017 Danone acquired WhiteWave and its plant-based brands, such as Alpro and Silk, taking the next step in offering more healthy choices to consumers and patients, and leading the way for flexitarian diets. 2023 Danone launched a new sustainability roadmap, the Danone Impact Journey. 1929 Daniel Carasso expanded Danone to France, maintaining the emphasis on the health benefits of yogurt while focusing also on taste. 2025 Danone achieves B Corp™ certification worldwide after a ten-year journey, a recognition that reflects sustained effort across subsidiaries in over 60 countries. 1919 Isaac Carasso founded Danone, driven by a mission to improve children's health. 1942 Daniel Carasso continued his father’s legacy by creating Dannon Yogurt in the US, laying the foundation for Danone’s global presence. 1972 Marseille speech - Antoine Riboud introduces the Dual Project, embedding social purpose into business strategy. Antoine Riboud and Daniel Carasso met for the first time in 1972, and soon after, they announced the merger of their two businesses. 2015 As proof of its commitment to people, communities, and the planet, Danone embarked on its journey to become one of the first globally B-Corp certified multinationals. 2020 Danone becomes the first listed company to adopt the "" Société à Mission "" status in France. 2006 The encounter between Franck Riboud and Nobel Prize winner Muhammad Yunus led to the creation in 2006 of world’s first corporate social business Grameen Danone Foods Ltd. Since then Danone has gone even further, with the creation of the impact investment fund Danone Communities (2007) Milestones that define us Certain moments stand out in Danone’s history, not just for what they achieved, but for what they revealed about the company’s character. 2026 Danone Impact Journey phase 2. 2009 Danone Ecosystem is created to empower communities, strengthen​ healthcare systems, and protect nature, through collaboration on projects with non-profit actors. 2011 Creation of the Livelihoods Carbon Fund, an impact investment fund dedicated to restoring natural ecosystems and delivering carbon credits. VISION HEALTH NATURE PEOPLE & COMMUNITIES GOVERNANCE INTEGRATED ANNUAL REPORT 2025 6"
2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf::chunk-13241,2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf,C3cd8894's 2025 Integrated Report,Danone,food_beverage,2025,integrated_or_annual_report,6,7,chunk-13241,5,,social,False,False,"of the Livelihoods Carbon Fund, an impact investment fund dedicated to restoring natural ecosystems and delivering carbon credits. VISION HEALTH NATURE PEOPLE & COMMUNITIES GOVERNANCE INTEGRATED ANNUAL REPORT 2025 6 DANONE AT A GLANCE Today, across our entire portfolio, we offer products tailored to the nutritional needs and eating habits of consumers at every stage of life. From baby formula that supports early development to specialized medical nutrition for patients with specific nutritional needs. From bottled water that provides safe hydration to essential dairy & plant-based products that balance nutrition, affordability, and taste. This breadth reflects both the diversity of human nutritional needs and Danone’s capacity to meet them through science, innovation, and scale. DANONE CATEGORIES ESSENTIAL DAIRY & PLANT- BASED PRODUCTS (EDP) Sitting at the heart of Danone’s heritage. We offer nutritious, delicious, and convenient choices, as well as tasty treats for moments of indulgence as part of a well‑balanced diet. Our diverse range of products supports gut health, immunity, or address the growing interest in high‑protein products. Alongside dairy, Danone’s plant‑based portfolio responds to consumers’ desire to diversify their diets, offering drinks and foods made from soy, almonds, oats and other ingredients, fortified with essential nutrients and designed to meet a wide range of dietary needs. SPECIALIZED NUTRITION (SN) We support people of all ages with specific nutritional needs, including babies and people with health conditions such as cancer or stroke. With over 125 years of expertise in Specialized nutrition, we develop pioneering products, services and educational programs to help families, caregivers, patients, and healthcare professionals make informed choices on nutrition and health. 27,283 total (in € millions) 34% 18% 48% WATERS We are determined to provide quality drinking water to as many people as possible while respecting our natural environment. Our portfolio of strong local and global products is highly differentiated. We have expanded our water range of plain sparkling and unsweetened options in new formats and business models to support people’s healthy hydration. In countries with safe tap water, our water brands, such as evian and Volvic, offer natural mineral waters known for their high quality and unique taste. In countries where safe drinking water is more limited, our brands like Bonafont in Mexico and AQUA in Indonesia provide access to safe drinking water. 27.3Bn€ SALES 90,000 NUMBER OF EMPLOYEES 151 sites PRODUCTION FACILITIES 120 countries GEOGRAPHIC REACH No. 1 worldwide for fresh dairy products & for plant-based foods and beverages in 2025 No. 2 worldwide for packaged waters in 2025 No. 2 worldwide for early life nutrition in 2025 No. 4 worldwide for adult medical nutrition in 2025 VISION HEALTH NATURE PEOPLE & COMMUNITIES GOVERNANCE INTEGRATED ANNUAL REPORT 2025 7"
2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf::chunk-13242,2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf,C3cd8894's 2025 Integrated Report,Danone,food_beverage,2025,integrated_or_annual_report,7,8,chunk-13242,6,,social,False,True,"No. 2 worldwide for early life nutrition in 2025 No. 4 worldwide for adult medical nutrition in 2025 VISION HEALTH NATURE PEOPLE & COMMUNITIES GOVERNANCE INTEGRATED ANNUAL REPORT 2025 7 +11.7% 14% OF SALES CHINA, NORTH ASIA & OCEANIA AMEA +5.6% 16% OF SALES EUROPE +2.3% 36% OF SALES NORTH AMERICA +2.0% 23% OF SALES OUR 2025 PERFORMANCE: KEY FACTS AND FIGURES Danone’s performance in 2025 reflected the strength of its strategic choices and the resilience of its business model. Like-for-like sales growth remained strong, margins improved through operational discipline, and investments in innovation and sustainability continued at pace. A global footprint that supports growth Danone’s business is distributed across five zones, each with distinct growth dynamics. This geographic diversity provides resilience against regional volatility and helps balance mature markets with higher-growth areas. LIKE-FOR-LIKE SALES GROWTH +4.5% VOLUME / MIX +2.7% RECURRING OPERATING INCOME €3,665m RECURRING OPERATING MARGIN 13.4% RECURRING EPS €3.80 RECURRING NET INCOME GROUP SHARE €2,461m FREE CASH FLOW €2.8bn ROIC 10.7% DIVIDEND PER SHARE €2.25 2025 key figures 2025 Like-for-like sales growth • Healthiest portfolio in the industry ranked #1 by the Access to Nutrition Index. • 87.8% of products rated ≥3.5 stars according to Health Star Rating System (volumes of dairy, plant-based, water & aquadrinks). • Sugar reduction 98.5% of our volumes of dairy and plant-based products aimed at children contained ≤10g of sugars per 100g of products. • Water access 24.7 million people provided with safe drinking water. • AAA Score by CDP for our environmental leadership and transparency. • Methane reduction #1 food company to align with the Global Methane Pledge. We have already reduced our methane emissions by 29.8% from fresh milk dairy supply in 2025 vs 2020. • Regenerative agriculture 42% of key ingredients were sourced directly from farms that have begun to transition. • Water stewardship 99.3% of production sites deployed 4R (Reduce-Reuse-Recycle-Reclaim) approach. PRESERVING AND REGENERATE NATURE PROGRESS & LEAD HEALTH THROUGH FOOD FOR CONSUMERS AND PATIENTS • Worldwide B Corp certification a 10-year journey completed."
2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf::chunk-13243,2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf,C3cd8894's 2025 Integrated Report,Danone,food_beverage,2025,integrated_or_annual_report,8,9,chunk-13243,7,,social,False,False,"of production sites deployed 4R (Reduce-Reuse-Recycle-Reclaim) approach. PRESERVING AND REGENERATE NATURE PROGRESS & LEAD HEALTH THROUGH FOOD FOR CONSUMERS AND PATIENTS • Worldwide B Corp certification a 10-year journey completed. • 98% of employees covered by Dan’Cares, Danone health protection and well-being program. • Living wage certified. THRIVING PEOPLE & COMMUNITIES LATIN AMERICA +6.0% 10% OF SALES Danone Impact Journey in 2025 +4.5% LFL sales growth in 2025, with growth in all regions Danone delivered VISION HEALTH NATURE PEOPLE & COMMUNITIES GOVERNANCE INTEGRATED ANNUAL REPORT 2025 8 RENEW DANONE: STRATEGIC PRIORITIES Launched in 2022, the Renew Danone strategy hase entered its second chapter. This phase builds on the foundations established in Chapter 1 while sharpening focus and raising ambition. In particular, Danone is projecting itself into the future of health and nutrition by transforming, whilst driving performance, with a clear focus on the following strategic areas. Doubling down on Renew Danone fundamentals Chapter 2 builds on the fundamentals re‑established between 2022 and 2024: reinforcing Danone’s ambition to fully play its role as a category leader, while continuing to invest in differentiating capabilities and maintaining strict discipline on cash and returns. It is also about further embedding and leveraging a genuine winning culture, grounded in science and innovation, operational and executional excellence, and proactive portfolio management. Pivoting the way we address our categories Danone is gradually pivoting the way it addresses its categories, looking at its markets in a consumer and patient-centric way, from yogurt to gut health and protein expertise, from plant-based to plant powered, from waters to healthy hydration. Within this framework, Danone is selectively strengthening its positioning in high protein and gut health offerings, leveraging its scientific capabilities and innovation engine across dairy, plant-based and specialized nutrition. In parallel, the Group is extending its patient journey by developing its presence in post discharge care and homecare."
2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf::chunk-13244,2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf,C3cd8894's 2025 Integrated Report,Danone,food_beverage,2025,integrated_or_annual_report,9,9,chunk-13244,8,,social,False,True,"scientific capabilities and innovation engine across dairy, plant-based and specialized nutrition. In parallel, the Group is extending its patient journey by developing its presence in post discharge care and homecare. Broadening some of our business models Danone is actively rebalancing its channel mix, further strengthening its presence in strategic channels (such as out-of-home, pharmacy and, foodservice). Together, these strategic channels represent over 50% of Danone’s sales and grew two to three times faster than mass retail in 2025. The away-from-home channel, including restaurants, cafes, hotels and workplaces, represents a significant growth opportunity. Consumers are increasingly eating and drinking outside their homes, and Danone is developing tailored products and partnerships to meet their needs. Medical nutrition is being strengthened through closer collaboration with healthcare systems, hospitals, and care facilities. This involves not only product innovation but also education, training, and evidence generation to support clinical adoption. Further expanding our geographic footprint Danone is pursuing disciplined geographic expansion, focusing on markets where the company can build sustainable positions over time. Danone will keep winning in the geographies where it is strong and has a balanced portfolio, like Europe, while expanding where its presence is narrower, such as in the US, but also catching some opportunities in geographies where it has low presence, such as India or South-East Asia. Further accelerating on portfolio management The Group has adopted a more balanced approach to portfolio management, becoming more active on acquisitions while remaining disciplined and applying clear strategic and financial criteria. In 2025, Danone notably acquired a majority stake in Kate Farms, a fast growing and #1 doctor-recommended plant- based medical nutrition brand in the U.S., and The Akkermansia Company (TAC), a Belgian company specializing in next generation biotic research. At the same time, Danone will continue to optimize its portfolio, in order to strengthen the Group in the long term. Building performance through people and leadership The successful execution of Renew Danone relies on strong people and leadership capabilities across the organization. Our People strategy is a key enabler of this ambition, empowering Danoners to drive performance, lead transformation and scale impact, ensuring that strategic priorities translate into consistent results across markets and categories, the Danone Way. Committed to a long-term value compounding model Danone aims to consistently deliver attractive returns, and expects, for the 2025-2028 period, like-for-like net sales growth between +3% and +5%, and recurring operating income to grow faster than sales. This financial guidance should allow Danone to deliver a structurally double-digit return on invested capital (ROIC) and progress towards its long-term ambition of sustainably delivering €3 billion free cash flow. This ambition reflect a commitment to sustainable, profitable growth that creates value for all stakeholders, shareholders, employees, customers, consumers, suppliers, and communities. VISION HEALTH NATURE PEOPLE & COMMUNITIES GOVERNANCE INTEGRATED ANNUAL REPORT 2025 9"
2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf::chunk-13245,2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf,C3cd8894's 2025 Integrated Report,Danone,food_beverage,2025,integrated_or_annual_report,9,10,chunk-13245,9,INTEGRATING SUSTAINABILITY IN OUR BUSINESS N A T H A L I E,social,False,True,"commitment to sustainable, profitable growth that creates value for all stakeholders, shareholders, employees, customers, consumers, suppliers, and communities. VISION HEALTH NATURE PEOPLE & COMMUNITIES GOVERNANCE INTEGRATED ANNUAL REPORT 2025 9 INTEGRATING SUSTAINABILITY IN OUR BUSINESS N A T H A L I E A L Q U I E R C H I E F S U S T A I N A B I L I T Y O F F I C E R Food is essential - and healthy food even more so. But we can only produce it if we protect the world it comes from. Our planet is facing growing challenges, and the food system we rely on is not fit for the future. It is impacting heavily the health, the resources of nature and people’s lives. This is why we are playing our part, true to Danone’s long-standing spirit of leading change, aiming to deliver lasting impact, at scale. To do so, we chose the solutions that are nature based, enhanced by pioneering technologies and lead with and by people - Danoners, farmers, communities... This is why we chose to focus on healthy products, produced in a sustainable way. After all, what is not sustainable does not last. This is why we will continue to bring Health Through Food to as many people as possible. Now, and for generations to come. DANONE IMPACT JOURNEY The Danone Impact Journey, launched in 2023, provides the strategic framework for translating sustainability commitments into action. It is organized around three interconnected pillars: Health Through Food, Nature, People & Communities. Each pillar contains selected priorities, and each priority is supported by specific targets with clear timelines and metrics. The structure is designed to be comprehensive but focused, covering the issues where Danone can make the greatest contribution. 2025: a milestone year 2025 represents a significant milestone in Danone’s sustainability journey. The results demonstrate consistent effort and meaningful impact. This performance reflects the role of governance - integrating sustainability into business – partnerships, resource allocation and culture, rooted in our purposeful legacy. This is why we reaffirm our sustainability ambition and step up our efforts for the next five years, with Danone Impact Journey phase 2. With and through our ecosystem of partners Danone is committed to generating a positive impact by aligning economic and social objectives, through continuous social dialogue and stakeholder engagement. Our approach to stakeholder engagement involves interacting with individuals and groups that both impact and are impacted by our value chain. This engagement enables us to understand diverse viewpoints and address community needs. It promotes value creation through dialogue, accountability, and transparency, aligning business practices with societal needs. Danone listens to and addresses stakeholder concerns, fostering trust and mutual respect. Watch the video VISION HEALTH NATURE PEOPLE & COMMUNITIES GOVERNANCE INTEGRATED ANNUAL REPORT 2025 10"
2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf::chunk-13246,2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf,C3cd8894's 2025 Integrated Report,Danone,food_beverage,2025,integrated_or_annual_report,10,11,chunk-13246,10,,environmental,False,False,"with societal needs. Danone listens to and addresses stakeholder concerns, fostering trust and mutual respect. Watch the video VISION HEALTH NATURE PEOPLE & COMMUNITIES GOVERNANCE INTEGRATED ANNUAL REPORT 2025 10 We have also worked with partners to build a more sustainable and resilient supply and production system. Our principle is to identify nature-based solutions, supported by technology where appropriate, to enable healthy ecosystems to produce efficiently and sustainably. In particular, we develop and promote regenerative agricultural models adapted to local realities, that help conserve and renew our planet’s resources, while improving farmers’ livelihoods. This supports our aim to mitigate and build resilience to climate change, which extends throughout our entire value chain, from farms to factories and beyond. We also seek to help improve overall water and land stewardship, including reducing the risk of deforestation and land conversion in watersheds and sourcing areas. For 30 years, we have been continuously evolving and shaping our portfolio, as we continue to help consumers to shift towards healthier and more sustainable diets. To keep our categories relevant and contribute to this shift, we work to ensure our products are nutritionally adequate and safe, have a low environmental impact, and remain economically fair and culturally acceptable to diverse local populations. DAIRY Fresh dairy products bring a great balance of nutritional density for their environmental impact, affordability and taste. Yogurt offers a wide range of essential nutrients and delivers multiple health benefits through its live bacterias and fermentation process - all while remaining one of the lowest-carbon options for animal-based protein. PLANT-BASED Low in saturated fats and a source of high-quality proteins and fibers, our plant-based products are specifically designed to support a wide range of dietary needs, with low carbon footprint by nature. Our core range of plant- based foods and beverages is fortified with 5 essential nutrients, such as calcium, iodine, vitamins B or D. WATER Water is the healthiest way to hydrate. We provide, and facilitate access to, high quality water, using mostly reusable jugs and 96% of of our bottles are recyclable. SPECIALIZED NUTRITION Specialized nutrition fulfils specific dietary needs and supports health in populations with unique nutritional requirements, such as babies, patients, or the elderly. We constantly innovate to optimize health outcomes with clinically proven solutions, building on decades of research. [1] WHO [2] Global Nutrition Report 2024 [3] GlobeScan, 2025 At Danone, we want to proactively adapt and contribute to more resilient food systems,"
2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf::chunk-13247,2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf,C3cd8894's 2025 Integrated Report,Danone,food_beverage,2025,integrated_or_annual_report,11,11,chunk-13247,11,,,False,False,"solutions, building on decades of research. [1] WHO [2] Global Nutrition Report 2024 [3] GlobeScan, 2025 At Danone, we want to proactively adapt and contribute to more resilient food systems, as it conditions our capacity to thrive as a business, and resonates with our DNA and dual project of sustainable financial and societal performance. Over the past 50+ years we have chosen to act where we can make a meaningful and lasting contribution to our business and to society. We have defined a clear purpose, which underpins our status of société à mission: bringing Health Through Food to as many as possible. Indeed, while the global food system has been successful in expanding access to nutrition and reducing hunger over the past 75 years, food and nutrition security are essential needs that remain at the heart of many of the challenges we face today. Current diets are considered as a major risk factor for non-communicable diseases worldwide[1], contributing to over $8 trillion annually in healthcare expenses and lost productivity. Malnutrition persists - over 2.2 billion adults are overweight[2] - food systems drive environmental degradation, while economic barriers to access healthy food remain severe and agricultural livelihoods are under pressure. ""Business-as-usual"" models show that these challenges and access to nutrition should aggravate everywhere. This makes Danone’s strategy, focused on it’s mission to bring heath though food, even more relevant. At Danone, we believe that food can be a key component of the solution, providing healthy diets produced by sustainable and equitable food systems. With humility yet determination we want to contribute to the transition, like many consumers and patients around the world[3]. Our sustainability strategy is designed to increase resilience and support both our societal impact and our business performance. In this way we can advance our purpose now, and for generations to come. Our conviction is that sustainability without performance has no impact, and performance without sustainability has no future. The next chapter of our Renew strategy builds upon our achievements so far and continues the discipline to deliver on the sustainability topics which carry impact, increase our resilience and bring compounding value to our competitiveness. In this context and building on great achievements in 2025, we reaffirm our sustainability ambition and step up our efforts for the next five years, with Danone Impact Journey phase 2. FOOD AS A FORCE FOR CHANGE VISION HEALTH NATURE PEOPLE & COMMUNITIES GOVERNANCE INTEGRATED ANNUAL REPORT 2025 11"
