2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf::chunk-13250,2025_integrated_report_c3cd8894.pdf,C3cd8894's 2025 Integrated Report,Danone,food_beverage,2025,integrated_or_annual_report,12,13,chunk-13250,14,,social,False,True,"dairy farmers and workers. [10] Enabling due diligence deployed in Danone operations. 2025 DANONE IMPACT JOURNEY PERFORMANCE DASHBOARD VISION HEALTH NATURE PEOPLE & COMMUNITIES GOVERNANCE INTEGRATED ANNUAL REPORT 2025 12 Entering into the Danone Impact Journey phase 2, we reaffirm our sustainability ambition and step up our efforts for the next five years, while ensuring Danone’s long-term resilience and competitiveness, and sustaining its growth trajectory. It is built on the same three pillars of action, with updated and expanded targets. In a fast-changing world, marked by evolving sustainability standards and expectations, local regulatory contexts and, above all, major challenges ranging from health burden to climate change, Danone chooses to further embed its sustainability priorities into its business by: • Pursuing consistently its efforts on 2030 targets • Extending the battles already achieved to push them one step further • Opening new battles that have a significant impact. Moreover, Danone will sustain some battles that have been achieved but require ongoing attention to preserve current progress and ensure targets remain at the achieved level. THRIVING PEOPLE & COMMUNITIES Reach ≥95% of eligible employees covered by the Dan’Life[11] program to support Danone employees at various life stages by end 2030, building on the pioneering DanCare[12] program and its successes Maintain 40-60% of women at all managers levels and foster gender progress in 1st Line Danone employees until 2030[13] Foster a unique, inclusive and diverse culture within Danone Allocate ≥30% of the total learning hours of Danone employees to the Future fit skills for sustainable growth, by end 2030 Upskill 10,000 Farmers & Workers In Dairy Supply Chain to improve farm resilience over the period 2025 -2030 Equip and empower employees and farmers with skills and capabilities of the future to develop in a fast-changing economy Reach ≥95% of Tier 1 suppliers[14] spend in scope of the Sustainable Sourcing Policy covered by Human Rights and Environmental Due Diligence (HREDD) by end 2030 Achieve and sustain certification as living wage employer by Fair Wage Network (FWN) until 2030 Champion a renewed social contract, upholding human rights and pursuing social progress TARGETS GOALS [1] Awaiting new SBTi standards, which may lead to adjusting current targets​. [2] Net Zero ambition is explained in §4.3.1 Climate change in Danone Universal Registration Document 2025.​ [3] The Danone Impact Journey Phase 2 target scope is revised to refocus on key ingredients with a climate, water and/or biodiversity risk. The Phase 2 target focuses on Direct Freshmilk (farmgate), Almonds, Direct Soy beans, Strawberry and Sugar beet in Europe that Danone sources directly from farmers or from suppliers working with farmers.​ [4] Danone Impact Journey phase 2 ambition is to extend the former target (covering Paper & Board, Palm, Soybean, Cocoa (direct cocoa & chocolate)) by adding new materials (coffee, soybean oil and beef) ​ [5] Thanks to the social businesses supported or previously supported by Danone Communities and the Water Access Acceleration Fund (W2AF).​ [6] Recover means recycle or valorize through energy recovery the equivalent amount by weight of plastic packaging put on the market. [7] Although the 2025 baseline already exceeds the 2030 target, the target aims to preserve and consolidate this strong performance, ensuring a predominantly healthy product portfolio. ​ [8] For each CBU is established the list of unique SKUs with their Weighted Distribution for the time period considered. For the 20% of SKUs having the highest values of Weighted Distribution, KPI, is considered the top quintile. Among this top list, is identified how many SKUs 