2025_sustainability_report_0478ad88.pdf::chunk-24579,2025_sustainability_report_0478ad88.pdf,0478ad88's 2025 Sustainability Report,ENGIE,utilities_energy,2025,clean_esg_or_sustainability_report,68,70,chunk-24579,34,,social,True,True,"FT-Statista 2025 Diversity Leaders ranking: ENGIE 78.53 (41/850 companies) Barometer on the representation of women in CAC 40 companies in 2024 : ENGIE N°1 Engie 2024 1.85% Target 2030 <2% 2024 ESG AT ENGIE EMPLOYEE BENEFITS Deployment achieved on the 4 pillars as of the end of 2024 100% of employees covered ENGIE CARE: The Social Protection Program For All Group Employees. Launch of a 5th pillar on mental health for deployment as of 2025 2024 Entities of the Group must ensure a minimum level of social protection for their employees by respecting each of the 4 pillars below: LIFE INSURANCE 12 months gross salary HOSPITALIZATION 75% of costs PARENTHOOD 14 weeks maternity leave 4 weeks paternity leave fully paid LONG TERM DISABILITY 12 months gross salary 69 ENGIE Care is the minimum level social of protection all over the Group : some Group entities go further on these four pillars and develop customised leave (adoption, infertility, endometriosis, menopause) or measures to support carers. ENVIRONMENT CLIMATE NATURE GENERAL INFORMATION SOCIAL SOCIETAL GOVERNANCE 2024 ESG AT ENGIE 70 EMPLOYEES COMMITMENT ENVIRONMENT CLIMATE NATURE GENERAL INFORMATION SOCIAL SOCIETAL GOVERNANCE % employees 2022 2023 2024 / 2025 Response rate 73% 78% 82% General Commitment Employees general commitment (index based on 8 questions) 86% 87% 87% Purpose “ I believe in the ability of the Group to accelerate the decarbonization of the economy” 80% 87% 88% Job satisfaction “My work gives me a sense of personal accomplishment” 83% 84% 85% Happiness at work “ I would recommend ENGIE as a good place to work” 85% 84% 85% Psychosocial risks “The stress levels at work are manageable” 75% 74% ENGIE & ME SURVEY An engagement survey launched in 2016 among the Group's employees worldwide 78 common questions to measure and analyse employees' perceptions of 7 different aspects of working life Conducted by ENGIE to gather feedback from employees about various aspects of their work environment and the Company’s strategy Aims to understand employee’s long-term commitment, confidence in the Group’s strategy and pride in contributing to it on a daily basis, job satisfaction and well being at work One set of questions in the survey is specifically aimed at well-being at work and the prevention of psychosocial risks. As of 2024 the ENGIE&Me survey becomes biennial to give more time to develop and implement actions plans"
2025_sustainability_report_0478ad88.pdf::chunk-24580,2025_sustainability_report_0478ad88.pdf,0478ad88's 2025 Sustainability Report,ENGIE,utilities_energy,2025,clean_esg_or_sustainability_report,70,71,chunk-24580,35,,governance,False,True,"specifically aimed at well-being at work and the prevention of psychosocial risks. As of 2024 the ENGIE&Me survey becomes biennial to give more time to develop and implement actions plans 2024 ESG AT ENGIE ▪Review the New H&S KPI included in managerial objectives ▪Deploy a vast training / coaching program from EXCOM to operational managers & include minimum mandatory H&S trainings for all Group employees inorder to permanently modify behaviors in front of risks ▪ Review consequence management approach (fair culture) to celebrate right actions and sanction more clearly risky behaviours. 71 ENGIE ONE SAFETY : OUR TRANSFORMATION PLAN TOWARDS THE GOAL OF ""ZERO SERIOUS INJURY AND FATALITY"" ENVIRONMENT CLIMATE NATURE GENERAL INFORMATION SOCIAL SOCIETAL GOVERNANCE THE TRANSFORMATION PLAN COVERS 7 AREAS: ▪Make sure Top management of the Group is committed and embodiesthis H&S Transformation Plan ▪Put in place acoordinated H&S management organization and governance at Group level ▪Put in place a management committee composed of H&S VP, Directors of H&S Departments, as well as H&S Directors of each GBU ▪Deﬁne Safety Essentials & mandatory, common rules and standards, applicable to all SAFETY CULTURE GOVERNANCE & ORGANIZATION ▪Deﬁne KPIs and reporting tools with a particular attention to leading indicators ▪Share and giveaccess to expertise, best practices, and tools to all entities RULES,STANDARDS, REPORTING, TOOLS ▪Set up an H&S pool of experts centered on the prevention of serious and fatal accidents directed by the H&SDepartment, to bring support and control close to the ﬁeld ▪Deﬁne the main missions and skills of the H&S functional line ▪Strengthen H&S Oversight and support in Procurement and Projects ▪Mobilize experts in caseof a severe injury or fatal accident SITE AUDITS& SUPPORT ▪Ensure that H&S resources are trained and motivated & deﬁne possible HR career paths to attract talents ▪Ensure H&S line works transversally H&S PEOPLE ▪Perform site audits and visits, including surveys of somebidders and contractors’ sites ▪Ensure the right ENGIE H&S supervision during projects’ execution CONTRACTING& PROJECTS ▪Define and set up a Group H&S strategic communication plan to support transformation and adhesion ▪Improve Safety awareness within the Group, from top management to the field ▪Set up H&S events to federate & motivate: Safety Week, Awards… COMMUNICATION & CHANGEMANAGEMENT 2022 2023 2024 REVIEW,REVISE, DEFINE,SETUP STEP UP,IMPLEMENT,TRAIN, CONTROL 2025 ANCHOR OBJECTIVE : ZERO SERIOUS INJURY AND FATALITY Sustainable eradication of serious and fatal accidents for all people working for the Group"
2025_sustainability_report_0478ad88.pdf::chunk-24581,2025_sustainability_report_0478ad88.pdf,0478ad88's 2025 Sustainability Report,ENGIE,utilities_energy,2025,clean_esg_or_sustainability_report,71,73,chunk-24581,36,,social,True,True,"2023 2024 REVIEW,REVISE, DEFINE,SETUP STEP UP,IMPLEMENT,TRAIN, CONTROL 2025 ANCHOR OBJECTIVE : ZERO SERIOUS INJURY AND FATALITY Sustainable eradication of serious and fatal accidents for all people working for the Group 2024 ESG AT ENGIE 72 ENGIE ONE SAFETY 2024 : MAIN RESULTS & ACHIEVEMENTS ENVIRONMENT CLIMATE NATURE GENERAL INFORMATION SOCIAL SOCIETAL GOVERNANCE Health & Safety performance indicators 2022 2023 2024 2024 TARGET 2030 TARGET Number of fatal accidents (employees, temporary workers and (sub)contractors) 4 6 3 0 0 Fatality rate for employees, temporary workers and (sub)contractors (per million worked hours) 0.014 0.019 0.009 0 0 Lost Time Injury Rate for employees, temporary workers and (sub)contractors (per million worked hours) 2.0 1.8 1.7 < 2.0 < 1.5 Continuation of « ENGIE One Safety Culture » training-coaching of managers New standards & technical instructions to prevent falls from height and to control electrical risks Organization of a yearly Safety Stand Down to commemorate the victims of fatal accidents and to reinforce the implementation of the Group’s expectations regarding the prevention of serious and fatal accidents New awareness-raising campaigns on 2 major risks and 2 Safety Essentials : • Control of risks associated with working at height • Electrical risk management • Systematic implementation of the Last Minute Risk Assessment before (re)starting an activity • Implementation of the “Stop the Work” procedure when safety conditions do not appear to be met Setting up of an “ENGIE One Safety"" website for the Group's various external stakeholders, in particular its subcontractors – presentation of ENGIE’s 5 Safety Essentials – possibility for subcontractors to follow a safety induction course to familiarize themselves with ENGIE’s Safety Essentials Main 2024 achievements https://onesafety.engie.com/ https://onesafety.engie.com/ 2024 ESG AT ENGIE 73 ENGIE ONE SAFETY CULTURE: TRAINING-COACHING FOR EFFECTIVE PRACTICE OF 5 MANAGERIAL SAFETY RITUALS ENVIRONMENT CLIMATE NATURE GENERAL INFORMATION SOCIAL SOCIETAL GOVERNANCE Simplified training for 7,000 functional managers (October 2023 - June 2025) Training and coaching for 10,000 operational managers Understanding the key principles 3 rituals to develop best practices on our sites 2 rituals to steer, act and support safety performance Health & Safety Tool Box Talk Safety Performance Review The Joint Safety Tour (subcontractor) The Life Saving Check The Managerial Safety Visit Approach focusing on the risks of serious and fatal accidents Providing managers with the tools and skills to increase their impact on operators' safety behaviour 8,578 managers trained 5,207 managers coached 2024"
