ical financial information (“ISAE 3000 (Revised)”), issued by the International Auditing and Assurance Standards Board. We believe that the evidence we have obtained is sufficient and appropriate to provide a basis for our opinion. Our responsibilities under this standard are further described in the Practitioner’s responsibilities section of our report. Our independence and quality management We have complied with the independence and other ethical requirements of the French Code of Ethics for Statutory Auditors (Code de Déontologie)"
